      "title": "👑 Pixaroma - Note - START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MODELS AND NODES USED IN THIS WORKFLOW  \n\n---\n\n### Models are downloaded automatically the first time you use the workflow.\n \n---\n\n## 🧩 Nodes Installed from Manager  \n\n- ComfyUI-Easy-Use\n- Qwen3-TTS - Voice Synthesis & Cloning\n\nRead More about Qwen TTS Node [HERE](https://github.com/flybirdxx/ComfyUI-Qwen-TTS)\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources  \n🎥 **Tutorials:** [Pixaroma YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma)  \n💬 **Community Discord:** [Join Here](https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3)\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Qwen3 Use Saved Voice Workflow\n\nGenerate speech using a voice you already saved with **SaveVoice**.\n\n### What it does\n- Loads a previously saved voice (**from models\\qwen-tts\\voices**)\n- Speaks your **Speech Text** using that saved voice\n- Saves an MP3\n\n### How to use\n1. **Load Previous Saved Voice (Press R to Refresh)**: select your saved voice file (example: `my_custom_voice.wav`).\n2. **Speech Text**: type what you want spoken.\n3. In **VoiceClone** set **language** to Auto or the correct language (English/Chinese).\n4. Click **Run**\n\n### Save location\n- Preview inside **Save Audio (MP3)**\n- File saves under: **ComfyUI\\\\output\\\\audio**"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
